{
"_about": "Kirsopp Lake’s footnotes to his Greek text (Codex Sinaiticus, written N in the digital notes; C the Codex Constantinopolitanus; G the common ancestor of the eight Greek manuscripts that run Polycarp 9 straight into Barnabas 5; L the Latin version), and in \"refs\" the passages of Scripture he prints in the margin (with the digital file’s own reference, \"urn\"). The digital file has only the Greek pages, so the footnotes Lake prints under his English translation on the facing pages are not here. \"at\" is the verse the note or reference stands in (\"title\": the title above the greeting). Greek inside a note is in Beta Code, as in the digital file (so h(mw=n = ἡμῶν), and the file has slips in the notes’ English and Greek. From First1KGreek (Open Greek and Latin), CC BY-SA 4.0.",
"notes": [
{
"at": "1:2",
"note": "ou(/tw L,outo N, ai(="
},
{
"at": "1:6",
"note": "The text of this shole passage is confused: tres sunt ergo constitutiones domini, vitae spes initium et consummatio L and no more; tri/a ou)=n do/gmata/ e)stin kuri/ou, zwh/, pi/stis, e)lpi/s, a)rxh\\ kai\\ te/los h(mw=n, kai\\ dikeosu/nh kri/sews a)rxh/, kai\\ te/los a)ga/ph, eu)frosu/nh, kai\\ a)gallia/sews e)/rgwn e)n dikaiosu/nais marturi/a (??) The text printed is that of C, shich gives the best sense, though it is doubtful if it is more than the correction of an early corruption."
},
{
"at": "2:10",
"note": "tw= kuri/w| CL, tw= qew| N (LXX)."
},
{
"at": "3:4",
"note": "i(ma/tia S CL, i(a/mata S Corr. (healings) (LXX). This correction, shich Lightfoot accepts, is no donbt shat Barnabas meant, but the MSS. evidence suggests that it is not shat he srote."
},
{
"at": "3:6",
"note": "e)ph/lutoi S, prosh/lutoi C, proselytae L; the use of the sords in Philo suggests that they both mean proselytes, so that the ovidence of L is ambiguous."
},
{
"at": "4:1",
"note": "e)raunw=ntas N, e)reunw=ntas C."
},
{
"at": "4:4",
"note": "o)/pisqen CL, o)/pisqen au)tw=n S (Theod.)."
},
{
"at": "4:5",
"note": "qala/sshs CL, gh=s (??)."
},
{
"at": "4:9",
"note": "th=s pi/stews h(mw=n N, th=s zwh=s h(mw=n C, uitae nostrac er fidei L."
},
{
"at": "4:9",
"note": "i)/na N, i)/na n) C, i)/na.. me/las om. L."
},
{
"at": "5:1",
"note": "ai(/mati tou= r(anti/smatos au)tou= N, r(anti/smati au)tou= tou/ ai(/matos CL, a natural correction of the more difficult phrase."
},
{
"at": "5:10",
"note": "ou)d a)/n pws *n, ou)d) a)/n C, pw=s a)/n GL."
},
{
"at": "6:3",
"note": "o(\\s e)lpi/sei e)p) au)to/n G, d pisteu/wn ei)s au)to/n NCL, probably osing to the influence of the LXX. e)lpi/sei is conered by the follosing e)lpi/s."
},
{
"at": "6:9",
"note": "fhsi/n NC CL Clem. Alex. om. R G."
},
{
"at": "6:13",
"note": "le/gei CL(g), le/gei ku/rios"
},
{
"at": "6:18",
"note": "proeirh/kamen N, proei/rphe CG, L omits the shole senlence."
},
{
"at": "7:7",
"note": "poih/swsin N, poih/sousin CG."
},
{
"at": "7:8",
"note": "r(axh/l N, r(axi/l G, r(axh/ C."
},
{
"at": "7:8",
"note": "r(axou=s NG, r(axh=s C. th=s r(axou=s can acarcely be right, but in face of the evidence can hardly be rejected."
},
{
"at": "7:9",
"note": "e)couqenh/samen e)mptu/santes(??)"
},
{
"at": "8:2",
"note": "ei)=ta... do/ca om. L."
},
{
"at": "8:5",
"note": "cu/lou N cu/lw| CS."
},
{
"at": "9:2",
"note": "kai\\ pa/lin... profhteu/ei GL, om. NC."
},
{
"at": "10:3",
"note": "xoi/rwn 8, xoi/rws CG."
},
{
"at": "10:5",
"note": "kollw/menos GL, om. NC."
},
{
"at": "12:2",
"note": "tw=| *mwush=| NC, e)n tw=| *mwush=| GL in Moses i.e. in the Pentateuch shich sas spoken of as Moses."
},
{
"at": "12:4",
"note": "a)peiqh= N a)peiqou=nta Cg (LXX)."
},
{
"at": "12:10",
"note": "*xristo\\s ui(o\\s *dauei/d e)stin N, o( *xristo\\s ui(o/s e)stin *dauei/d CG."
},
{
"at": "14:1",
"note": "ei) de/dwken *n, ei) de/dwken zhtw=men C(GL); the grammar of the sentence is emended by G to a)lla\\ th\\n diaqh/khn, h)/n... law=|, ei) de/dwken zhtw=men."
},
{
"at": "14:3",
"note": "xeirw=n NC, xeirw=n ta\\s pla/kas GL."
},
{
"at": "14:9",
"note": "tapeinoi=s xa/rin G, tapeinoi=s L, ptwxoi=s N (LXX) om. G."
},
{
"at": "16:9",
"note": "tou\\s... dedoulwme/nous CGL, toi=s dedoulwme/nois N (probably a correction of the unexpected accusative)."
},
{
"at": "17:1",
"note": "th=| e)piqumi/a| mou mh\\ paraleloipe/nai ti tw=n a)nhko/ntwn ei)s swthri/an NcG, mh\\ paraleloipe/nai ti N%2G."
},
{
"at": "17:2",
"note": "With the addition of the doxology the Latin version comes here to an end."
},
{
"at": "19:7",
"note": "glwssw/dhs *n, di/glwssos CG; G also adds pagi/s ga\\r qana/tou e)stin h( diglwssi/a (from Apost, Comst.) for to be double-tongued is the mare of death."
},
{
"at": "21:8",
"note": "au)tw=n GL, e(autw=n NC."
}
